From 3abc58fb27b4201d39a581ceb06bb62eafcd999b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:36:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] coordination: derive claims from registered repository
 identities

Ordinary registration now resolves its canonical bare clone, real common
Git directory and normalized SSH origin without requiring a catalog entry.
Keep configured mappings as consistency checks and preserve an explicit
registered default branch, including main, without granting merge authority.

Resolve Git outside the ledger mutex and recheck bounded local identity
proofs at admission. Exact request retries return retained records before
looking for a clone; queued grants keep their frozen resource keys.

Advertise dynamic repository support in a separate immutable capability.
Package selection validates every held or waiting repository against its
retained resources and refuses incapable or remapped candidates. Existing
claim records, legacy capability equality and machine catalogs stay intact.
