From 9b5db67dd0e55029728885b835d50c543c3f3d75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Skokan <jakub.skokan@havefun.cz>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:45:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] portal: measure read stages without logging session
 content

Expose local correlation tokens and numeric Server-Timing for selected
non-streaming read lanes. Measure existing verification and details
boundaries and limits-cache waits without changing authority or budgets.

Rate-limit slow/error records across the portal and use fixed lane,
stage and cancellation labels. Keep identifiers, paths, payloads and raw
errors out of these records. Admission and native connection/write waits
remain explicitly unmeasured rather than inferred from total latency.
---
 docs/workspace-portal.md                     |  10 ++
 portal/internal/web/codex_limits.go          |   4 +
 portal/internal/web/codex_providers.go       |   1 +
 portal/internal/web/read_diagnostics.go      | 172 +++++++++++++++++++
 portal/internal/web/read_diagnostics_test.go | 109 ++++++++++++
 portal/internal/web/server.go                |  41 ++++-
 6 files changed, 331 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 portal/internal/web/read_diagnostics.go
 create mode 100644 portal/internal/web/read_diagnostics_test.go

diff --git a/docs/workspace-portal.md b/docs/workspace-portal.md
index 55613a1..9c56356 100644
--- a/docs/workspace-portal.md
+++ b/docs/workspace-portal.md
@@ -380,6 +380,16 @@ keep the existing refresh behavior.
 Team status unavailable marks stale peer-activity observations. A successful
 HTTP response clears it only when the returned observations are fresh.
 
+Instrumented non-streaming read responses include `X-Portal-Read` for correlation
+and numeric `Server-Timing` stages. Timings cover the measured lookup, verification and details dependencies;
+nested stages overlap. Limits-cache waits are measured separately. Admission and
+native connection/write waits remain unmeasured. Slow or failed reads emit at most
+one `portal_read` log record per second across the portal. These records contain
+fixed lane/stage names, durations, status and cancellation category, without
+session or native identifiers, paths, queries, request/response contents or error
+text. Response timing ends when headers are written; the log total includes the
+handler's completion. These diagnostics do not change authority or time budgets.
+
 Index snapshot warnings use the same grace period as failed HTTP refreshes,
 including when the server successfully returns its last known state. Repeated
 warnings do not restart the grace period. A healthy snapshot clears the warning.
